<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">Taifa of Morón</h1><p class="st-meta">1013 CE – 1066 CE (approx.) · capital Morón de la Frontera</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Berber principality around Morón de la Frontera, one of the small hill-town states between Seville and Ronda that the Abbadids absorbed.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Around 1013 the Banu Dammar, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> clan whose soldiers had served the Córdoban <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphs</a>, took control of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moron-de-la-frontera">Morón</a> and its district in the countryside south-east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seville">Seville</a> under Nuh ibn Abi Tuziri al-Dammari.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moron-de-la-frontera">Morón</a> was a modest state built around a castle, olive groves and grain land. Its rulers allied with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hammudid-dynasty">Hammudids</a> and the other <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taifa">taifas</a>, such as the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/taifa-of-carmona">Taifa of Carmona</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/taifa-of-ronda">Taifa of Ronda</a>, against the expanding Arab dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seville">Seville</a>. Little is known of its administration.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1066 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-mutadid-of-seville">al-Mutadid</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/taifa-of-seville">Taifa of Seville</a> annexed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moron-de-la-frontera">Morón</a>, reportedly after luring <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> rulers into a trap. The town remained Muslim until the Castilian conquest in the 13th century.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/taifa-of-moron.jpg" alt="Taifa of Morón" width="320" height="271"><figcaption>Image: Tyk · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Location_map_Taifa_of_Mor%C3%B3n.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1013 CE – 1066 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Morón de la Frontera</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Nuh ibn Abi Tuziri, Muhammad ibn Nuh</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Andalusi Arabic, Berber</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Morón</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1040&amp;focus=taifa-of-moron" aria-label="Taifa of Morón on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4543 841 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Taifa of Morón lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4863 1097L4881 1071M4863 1097L4850 1088"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4881 1071h0M4850 1088h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4863 1097h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4863 1097h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Morón de la Frontera. <a href="/atlas?year=1040&amp;focus=taifa-of-moron">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
